  "note": "The historic Al-Sarafiya Bridge crosses the Tigris on two high steel through-trusses and a lower central span. Open cross-bracing, pale gray lattice, red-and-white road separators, sidewalks and the long approach spans follow the photographed bridge. Both deck ends meet the sampled native roads at their mapped joins. The central deck clears the native Tigris water and the pier bases extend into the sampled terrain. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
